Contributing to HPINDAC
Thanks for taking a look. Here's the honest, direct version of how to get involved.
Where things actually stand
This is a pre-audit, testnet-only project, built by two non-technical founders, now looking for real developer collaboration to take it further. Nothing here
is production-ready — see CHANGELOG.md and the known limitations listed in each issue
for exactly what that means in practice.
The fastest way in: pick an issue
Check the Issues tab — each one is scoped, specific, and tagged help wanted.
They range from small (a good first look at the codebase) to substantial (real architectural
judgment calls). Pick whichever matches your interest and comment on it before starting, so
we're not duplicating effort.
If you want to do a deeper review instead
Open a new issue, or just comment directly on any existing one — we're genuinely glad to
hear "this part is wrong" as much as "here's a fix." Both are valuable.
What working with us looks like right now
No cash upfront. We're pre-funding, two founders, fully transparent about it. Real
contributions are discussed on a milestone — happy to talk specifics
directly.
You get to evaluate the project and us before anything's locked in, and vice versa.
Security-first, always. If a proposed change touches deposit, redemption, fee, or
custody logic, hope real honesty, verify and valuable contributions.
How to reach us
Open an issue, comment on an existing one, or reach out directly — contact details are in
the repo profile.
Why this might be worth your time
Hedera doesn't yet have a native version of the "vault factory" infrastructure model that
Reserve Protocol has proven at scale elsewhere. If bridge-free architecture, immutable core
logic, or oracle security design interests you, this is a genuinely early, real opportunity
to shape something from close to the ground up — not just implement a finished spec.
